# Sourced by pi-gen's build.sh rather than executed, so it carries no shebang.
# shellcheck shell=bash
#
# Every assignment here is read by the sourcing script, never by this file.
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
# pi-gen configuration for the mtrack image. Copied into a pi-gen checkout as
# ./config; see packaging/pi-gen/README.md.

IMG_NAME='mtrack'
PI_GEN_RELEASE='mtrack multitrack player'

# Raspberry Pi OS release to build against. pi-gen's package sets differ per
# release, so building an older one means checking out the matching pi-gen
# branch as well -- and it has to stay one of the arm64 branches, since ARCH is
# selected by branch rather than by anything settable here. The README covers it.
RELEASE="${RELEASE:-trixie}"

# The whole point of shipping avahi: this is what answers to mtrack.local.
TARGET_HOSTNAME='mtrack'

# Lite plus our stage. Nothing here wants a desktop, and stage2 must not export
# an image of its own -- the workflow drops SKIP/SKIP_IMAGES files to arrange
# that. MTRACK_STAGE_DIR is an absolute path into this repo, which pi-gen
# supports for stages outside its own tree.
STAGE_LIST="stage0 stage1 stage2 ${MTRACK_STAGE_DIR:?MTRACK_STAGE_DIR must point at packaging/pi-gen/stage-mtrack}"

DEPLOY_COMPRESSION='xz'
COMPRESSION_LEVEL=6

# On a machine with no monitor, ssh is the recovery path. It is only useful
# once an account exists, which is the next comment's business.
ENABLE_SSH=1

# Deliberately no FIRST_USER_PASS, and DISABLE_FIRST_BOOT_USER_RENAME left off.
# pi-gen then leaves the account locked and runs the setup wizard on first
# boot, so this image ships with no default credentials for anyone to guess.
# The headless path is Raspberry Pi Imager's customisation, which writes the
# username, password, wifi and ssh keys onto the boot partition before the card
# is ever booted; the README says so, because a reader who does not know that
# will conclude the image is broken.

# Likewise no WPA_COUNTRY: wifi stays rfkill'd until a country is set, and
# Imager sets it. Hardcoding one here would be wrong everywhere but there.
